#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "354142ae-6999-5699-b81d-9f16570b6115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-12x+25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327394} {:answer/id #uuid "6637b75c-a39e-5721-a28b-4a320ad5c971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=12x-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327821} {:answer/id #uuid "790d805f-3881-5904-ba81-7ea14a53c052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-3x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327971} {:answer/id #uuid "85aa1fa8-f1d2-5839-ba72-e02c15010a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-4x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328087} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf17a1f-abef-5a3c-bb11-4d68176c30e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=4x-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328579}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186327821} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f94fd28-0c54-584b-93ad-2ea2c59a1f97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6c44e7b4-d61a-54f6-b052-1c62e5ff035f" :question/math-academy-id "q-48666" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(5-3x)}^{4},$ find the equation of the tangent at point $(2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={g}^{4},\\,g=5-3x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4{g}^{3},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4{g}^{3}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-12(5-3x)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & =-12{(5-3(2))}^{3} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(2,1)$ is $m=12.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =12(x-2) \\\\ y-1 & =12x-24 \\\\ y & =12x-23\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332659 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b827063-1d46-592f-9069-3390743f7989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330049} {:answer/id #uuid "6e43e3f4-8303-527b-ac9c-0202bbca05b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\text{arcsec}\\,x-2{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330942} {:answer/id #uuid "acc6d2b2-c8da-5516-a0d3-c4774188c11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\text{arccot}\\,x-{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331480} {:answer/id #uuid "c08add0e-78e7-54c5-ab17-51b762ee0b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331658} {:answer/id #uuid "dffe2f36-c755-5d60-bf8f-1aebfadb9e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-2{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331928}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330049} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8440b49-5a42-5c64-b1d3-8c392b4f068f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "58be8fc4-bf7c-5658-9dd6-29f09252f095" :question/math-academy-id "q-49075" :question/problem "If ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+1}-4{x}^{3},$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+1}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 4{x}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {x}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08b5c003-977b-526c-9170-9794348054d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-2{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330027} {:answer/id #uuid "248f8453-3a33-57da-89df-9bf51e524234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{ arcsec }x+4{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330261} {:answer/id #uuid "43e2ebab-bd93-5d5d-a12b-e839363c1d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330558} {:answer/id #uuid "bf520213-de34-5d15-a3a8-4acc7d0a6455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-2{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331646} {:answer/id #uuid "d44450f0-95d3-5bbf-9bc3-9c36dc4e5fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\text{ arcsec }x-4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331833}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330027} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fa5dfcc-f8bf-57f0-80c1-40fef676854d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1473ed23-4c35-5374-b722-df11f2918a3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49129" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-6\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-2{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43890837-0184-542e-bfb0-c8abf26f2d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\text{ arcsec }x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330556} {:answer/id #uuid "87f58c01-b83d-5223-a5c6-46b3cb72b81f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331162} {:answer/id #uuid "c6950c18-8dd3-5690-bea9-67e9c321a527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331709} {:answer/id #uuid "d79dbd64-34c7-5d4e-a3a7-0728a5eba915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331856} {:answer/id #uuid "f4449f42-3c0a-590e-aa9c-1d1fc42bb400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332101}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331856} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c19e67a-f86d-502d-a731-a117cbd29d2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7235061c-31e7-5f21-9e2a-41d26e24ad09" :question/math-academy-id "q-49131" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (\\frac{4}{1+{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{4}{1+{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332665 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27b0389e-1d57-5284-9063-eafd54da004e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\text{ arcsec }x-9x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330304} {:answer/id #uuid "76836d51-9788-55ab-8819-9f6ac5535b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-9{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331011} {:answer/id #uuid "868330b0-f4a0-5fcd-8886-75cb323c4dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-9x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331145} {:answer/id #uuid "8fb21daf-d4d6-5218-8b4b-ffea684f82e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x-4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331224} {:answer/id #uuid "d9a8ea66-f445-58de-98b4-e7a240fb7b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+3{x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331882}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331145} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8706d15-624e-5108-a410-67cf897b31bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7f0fd041-ce90-54f7-824e-5b0234fc7192" :question/math-academy-id "q-49133" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (\\frac{6}{1+{x}^{2}}-9)\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{6}{1+{x}^{2}}-9)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 9\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x-9\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-9x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46505b2f-1953-51c1-89b1-262c3e1e114f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\text{ arcsec }x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330584} {:answer/id #uuid "53ca920a-4368-56bd-b725-1abcf2b6713e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330708} {:answer/id #uuid "61645379-6ba4-5686-88be-a9d0c67ea769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330813} {:answer/id #uuid "927c467d-2be8-5aa7-9b42-5199a503c166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\text{ arcsec }x-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331254} {:answer/id #uuid "a6184f98-47c2-57d1-922d-d6ecf85d4ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\text{ arcsec }x-3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331435}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330584} :answer-field/id #uuid "9269b8e4-4637-529d-ad83-2e10b9866149" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "93133dfc-bc5a-589b-9b21-0d9909f27fa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-49136" :question/problem "If ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\text{ arcsec }x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332667 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15842927-5e4a-5e46-9127-104f316af131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330123} {:answer/id #uuid "41bc032e-a7e4-523f-af57-7bedde2ea236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330533} {:answer/id #uuid "5725f42c-d6dd-585b-b6e2-2c205d9241ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-8\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330730} {:answer/id #uuid "8585560a-8491-5f60-8ffc-92f27c87fff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331134} {:answer/id #uuid "b646879c-4463-5645-8b8e-07c71a52b0f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8x+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331558}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330730} :answer-field/id #uuid "16671cae-c5b7-5203-87f8-f4d93fa21ee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4c5875e3-9603-540e-a71c-3edccf17389a" :question/math-academy-id "q-49150" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{{x}^{2}-7}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit  to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-7}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+1-1-7}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)-8}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}+1}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}+1}}-\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C,\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1-\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{8}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x-8\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-8\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097973d9-9ded-556a-9845-2e01f4285582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/5c/5c933988eb335b7310387cfc532a6e144de3e43bfebde4c29d1e5fe76fa35027.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330031} {:answer/id #uuid "7df61f71-c57b-5b3a-bb1e-71c5faddfe2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4a/4a2aefaff6332175608a37f6532bafd5be4ccb60a2aad8e4400a0f5767c4588a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331057} {:answer/id #uuid "ae78f203-25a9-5c21-a930-c1db83c7064a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/aa/aae99f368b61351b9163646b70ea0b085019d6935334422ccb398958a81d1e47.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331492} {:answer/id #uuid "d249f656-2f38-5318-b289-f42310bd1132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/76/763db9d469cdd9047ec823966fc922726c97cb22e6cd848a432f26bc5e6529d6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331816} {:answer/id #uuid "f90cf1a3-9d3e-5917-a76d-9ba382f31925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/89/8910d0342d03d546117091ccd19378905b8cfc3644997cfe3ca7d95a3b4e7a6f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332139}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330031} :answer-field/id #uuid "b60cced6-9db4-5c73-bcb1-9ed58f36cdd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "70caacc2-c352-5e5b-80a4-9b13475ccda0" :question/math-academy-id "q-49947" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ for $x>0?$" :question/worked-solution "Rearranging and Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C,\\,x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,2.$\n\n![](images/8e/8e047c3c27a000af943f50499f8c7559acceeb78cc006e796c7d353729991517.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332796 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c2556ab-42eb-5b03-9b82-ffafb8c7bdf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=6{x}^{3}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330340} {:answer/id #uuid "340e3d02-facf-523f-89ff-093dd1bcd18f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-2{x}^{2}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330411} {:answer/id #uuid "aae0e4e4-5033-5e88-827b-62d31ab7b6e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331464} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f11883-6eaf-55d0-bcf4-0414977256ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332068} {:answer/id #uuid "fdcec268-59b1-5bae-be4e-f748d99e9108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{3}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332183}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332183} :answer-field/id #uuid "9815a89d-855b-59fa-9302-62052d559095" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "860439d5-1eb6-58cf-8abd-cc9242b3ec59" :question/math-academy-id "q-50044" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=2$\n \n\n$$\nx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6{x}^{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =6\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=2{x}^{3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(-1)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =2(-1)^{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =-2+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{3}+4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332799 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a8cac35-ec47-5085-bcb0-da00cb39efe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330181} {:answer/id #uuid "2ecb6c15-4ffb-53a5-a6a3-acd959f971df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330360} {:answer/id #uuid "82e52b8f-937b-5b6c-bf07-b2a4477afeb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331109} {:answer/id #uuid "d1cbd642-0604-55df-9d4b-e311b2299017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-{x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331810} {:answer/id #uuid "f83e9e7e-87a9-5751-b17a-60d01d2b92ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330360} :answer-field/id #uuid "75e80a73-b1ef-545c-bc47-759f5717a078" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8704e7df-0e87-5dd2-a140-acb85a41ea4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-50092" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1.$\n\n$$\n2x+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}+4x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}+2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(1)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}+{1}^{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{4}{3}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3120f347-6512-51ba-8814-9e94e5b4f3e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330382} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce95280-683d-5e12-8dc4-4bd3c4dab2ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330490} {:answer/id #uuid "3f867192-f0f3-5837-8919-076f5a3bf835" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330514} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3c8989-f6d0-5647-ba9e-eebb2011d570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332030} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd989d0-88b5-5bdf-841b-6beef220f5ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={x}^{4}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C{x}^{2}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332184}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330490} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc205ab-aa57-5042-9e55-6ce79c5b03ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6d572743-1005-5db1-a849-a7030811290a" :question/math-academy-id "q-50146" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $x\\cdot \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-4x.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)-4\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88dad183-ed2b-5a15-83b8-2f429e39030d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331167} {:answer/id #uuid "963a6dbf-bdcb-54b7-b515-ded61ba89b6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331284} {:answer/id #uuid "bafaabc4-4fca-516b-a9d6-7ed9697af49a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331598} {:answer/id #uuid "fd70074b-45df-5d86-ae50-06ecb0063c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x)=2x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332179} {:answer/id #uuid "ffdab17a-cdb5-59fe-8492-3c8a1b66fd32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}+x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332199}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331284} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c1e6eb7-20e6-5c26-9817-474a9a29bb18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ab41d9c4-5e4f-5845-a572-d7bd4049e427" :question/math-academy-id "q-50159" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-2.$\n\n$$\n(1+2x){f}^{′}(x)-2=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{1+2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=(1+2x).$ Then $\\text{d}u=2\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int \\frac{2}{1+2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|+C \\\\ -2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2\\cdot 0|+C \\\\ -2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|+C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2x|-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332808 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a36ddfca-2b14-509d-b5d4-e1b9e7e3d77a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/36/3670e1b40ce25af5974059a86c502cfb68f80e81746cbb162805ab7ae4a6bce2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331414} {:answer/id #uuid "cb41bf96-b7f8-5841-b2a3-e61783f9e2c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/1c/1cf05351f0353e95dbdff8f620f6e920650d505be88edb3e61486676cb59357c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331752} {:answer/id #uuid "d493a642-0802-5e9f-bbcf-6f942159881d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/7d/7d23f940448475b1da1008ab1d3270236abec662208e81bd0de9355e85103a38.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331835} {:answer/id #uuid "df729bef-a2ff-5cbe-8c4a-710c0ea5cca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/90/90beec07c4d15fa823aee98c8a1a1e6c58846bb9b713b84848e010cc98cb3ca3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331922} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f097f0-5895-56e1-86a8-3d39d336d5d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/18/18a0a935932bbe409ceb7e36459a2091ee46b74829c873bfc048a71f543d8eff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331948}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331922} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9ca8b77-7e7d-5a41-bcb5-89f345e28085" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "33315476-f420-5411-98c9-f5414bf3df7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-50197" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+1=0$ for $x>0?$" :question/worked-solution "Rearranging and Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1$ for $x>0.$\n\n![](images/c8/c837c3b617fa49f3d081d961196a954fada99b8d7cd12b7d7f729232e16be066.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045fe77f-3730-5d18-925c-cda953523ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d2/d29058f4c71941f04dd2d934f1896972f0eb41a179984ec5d3675265ee9da56c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329995} {:answer/id #uuid "105c00ce-00da-5bc3-8cf5-f61420a4738b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/25/25e8c2c60a948d324dc7b836815e81a0321b1353dafded0c789d53b9c73d5edc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330094} {:answer/id #uuid "618d5040-e32c-5a5e-a2bf-f639bcfc73b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/5e/5e94f63a81cee566fea810265d8a37959617abaf5a8c50250c269fe44584405e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330817} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8ed54a-35d6-5d38-b1f1-c0de7905f0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/93/93c572ba14dadbcabaf218f2395d51465ceef24d1c7c4083025ea67bb36ed438.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331911} {:answer/id #uuid "e5cf4c06-f247-5d6d-8b9f-b702c5060f68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/81/81cc65015383f5c4b749a716d15b991d5a14d50d79aa866de22b41de0d802e53.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331974}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329995} :answer-field/id #uuid "a52669b3-0765-547b-b498-ecf9824e35ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a9ab5d27-4252-558a-bd60-3bb29dff9bd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-50198" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-3,0,3.$\n\n![](images/2d/2d64c09661973b7ef840e783a88de85d5ca9cf3436fae7eaebef36aca98ae631.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332811 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4267cc-bd1e-507b-8072-2b2a8c2eca09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330502} {:answer/id #uuid "8b417cb4-a6eb-5024-a1dc-ec0c00436d6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331187} {:answer/id #uuid "a75d6c04-3e75-57b3-9835-3be982051f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331442} {:answer/id #uuid "bea71f13-c9fb-5f86-9a53-ebbcbb8c38fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331639} {:answer/id #uuid "ee34aca2-9235-5324-8e51-2b3c711ec180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332039}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331639} :answer-field/id #uuid "d34e31ac-faf7-57f2-94a5-145454205303" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "35b7f010-fdff-57b3-be05-b9c6b80db56c" :question/math-academy-id "q-50220" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{1}{1+C} \\\\ 1+C & =1 \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332825 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42390f84-76dd-513e-bfe6-30ef499d0b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330541} {:answer/id #uuid "551e91b4-3be3-55eb-845f-b95b7bb7e037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-y=\\sqrt{x+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330716} {:answer/id #uuid "625cb73d-fe58-5029-93a5-e925201b1fec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-y=\\sqrt{2x+7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330831} {:answer/id #uuid "a48b421b-d946-5b0e-a7fc-5f7cf21d83e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331427} {:answer/id #uuid "b2fdf6fa-d413-5479-9d2f-edfcccbd37ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331529} :answer-field/id #uuid "47c02f84-950c-5f01-8fca-af4deaa528ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "11569a87-05ce-5134-b8db-439ec10012e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-50566" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x$  that satisfies  $y(-3)=1.$  Assume that $y>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x \\\\ \\int y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+2{C}_{1} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2{C}_{1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $y>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(-3)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+C} \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{9+C} \\\\ C & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x$ that satisfies the condition $y(-3)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0f0659a-f269-52ef-b304-c23cad84d0ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331661} {:answer/id #uuid "ca35de27-d1e1-59d0-a2a9-f78785b1444e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={x}^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331740} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b4f4c9-b558-5ee4-a800-ef30f1c79326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{6x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331982} {:answer/id #uuid "f2c90cf3-26dd-5a81-914f-55f2cb12af11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=(6x+C)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332088} {:answer/id #uuid "f83e8a13-c62b-51fd-8ed2-ddfc18d4dd51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332130}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331661} :answer-field/id #uuid "441c0ad2-d7c0-5882-98f9-ea5796307051" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a67e182b-8e5b-5502-83c8-9d36e701587d" :question/math-academy-id "q-51256" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6x\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6x\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\cdot 3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\int {y}^{-2/3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{1/3} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{1/3}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335737 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dafe268-bb8a-597a-bc86-bb319556af55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{-x}+4{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333568} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb03da1-870f-5e36-9071-60c94ef4942b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333826} {:answer/id #uuid "93c51a10-13c5-5dc3-affa-5c2e7e487d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}-3{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334304} {:answer/id #uuid "aaae8f7a-ee6d-5859-b1d3-3313fac24cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334485} {:answer/id #uuid "e9662fca-8c99-5f7b-850c-9aa6cdbae508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335031}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334485} :answer-field/id #uuid "60d56ba9-1ce9-5469-9145-c13a9aea9733" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "29ee4fe8-3de9-5ffb-adea-6b9fd8781620" :question/math-academy-id "q-64706" :question/problem "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}-3y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-3{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -3)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =3.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-x}$ and ${e}^{3x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $-5{e}^{-3x}$ is not a solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b8de8f1-0aa5-5597-8f2a-04314cbb183e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333095} {:answer/id #uuid "15516e59-127e-5585-b223-c41ec895f21c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333176} {:answer/id #uuid "852d9dce-fad7-5d6d-9d52-31ed637d34a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334173} {:answer/id #uuid "8936b9da-7dc8-5edc-ba5b-5f96a52fcf44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334208} {:answer/id #uuid "e05757f5-0bd3-5d05-a456-6e255ec4d863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334942}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334942} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b23fc9c-30a6-50f5-8daf-56d713fe0638" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e41bd3a2-77cd-50f9-af0d-7902e2113a96" :question/math-academy-id "q-64747" :question/problem "Compute the Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ for ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ of two functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ is defined as:\n\n$$\nW({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=\\begin{vmatrix}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{vmatrix}={y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{x}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =({e}^{x}){(x{e}^{x})}^{′}-(x{e}^{x}){({e}^{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})({e}^{x}+x{e}^{x})-(x{e}^{x})({e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({e}^{x}+x{e}^{x}-x{e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447870c5-0e16-591a-8300-97b1a1b53090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$14$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333622} {:answer/id #uuid "548b03ca-4238-5b00-9cb4-91def2cc07cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$14\\sqrt{2}$ and $4\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333761} {:answer/id #uuid "68381630-1c58-5c47-b731-887a1f1decb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$7$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333945} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa132ec-2b5e-506f-9009-d06c05f62c18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$7$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333966} {:answer/id #uuid "f94f55ce-3720-511d-baaa-529e5639ba46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$7\\sqrt{2}$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335173}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333622} :answer-field/id #uuid "c27addb0-e02b-555b-8abb-615b89631ce7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "50aac069-cc6f-51ae-b729-84e72b0989dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-69563" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=49.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=49,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20394717-12ca-5041-b23f-416aa83995b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333278} {:answer/id #uuid "45f72ead-a726-5b03-9e54-669f062a7bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333636} {:answer/id #uuid "5efc1e85-e466-5527-bfee-b216fc63bee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333854} {:answer/id #uuid "6f183c3b-27ac-5c2a-91b0-f1eac914fd3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334001} {:answer/id #uuid "7c2e1340-0645-5d50-95ed-65fc11a6a4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334099}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333854} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a765e3d-d8c0-512a-9934-b557f6c6eeaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e2872275-2ccf-570a-873b-56e8f9665a65" :question/math-academy-id "q-69891" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9eb144bd4109846f3e1af4fb7d8ed70d2d8a29c3804547b89238d6437c4258d8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b3bb62-33b0-5fec-8deb-ae6cde1bb204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333142} {:answer/id #uuid "57b12094-7cc6-57f1-9a04-7d107daa9163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333789} {:answer/id #uuid "723d2d46-f03f-5f70-9a86-d1649d7ce1a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334024} {:answer/id #uuid "c1a9b15c-1941-5024-81d9-ee6347a6b3e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334669} {:answer/id #uuid "ff431699-49d9-55e7-9957-c34cb6f5df16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335235}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335235} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfa364a8-de07-5a0a-aec8-fc0fb7bebdf9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "daa08063-18f2-5c3f-bfa5-03e9e47d2153" :question/math-academy-id "q-69892" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1acc2d6b8387947ff7186322796e273bcec366810ad73ac0025494ab627e06b2.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=1$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01216287-0f50-583c-9086-c9c0e4cc5138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332999} {:answer/id #uuid "308f5905-a1ef-5cd4-bcbf-93f14e467471" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333438} {:answer/id #uuid "853926c0-f101-5e2d-baf4-3a46b814eb53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334174} {:answer/id #uuid "8ca9f7c3-1c08-5f19-869f-2b8bb488f6c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334242} {:answer/id #uuid "e9a37e6e-54ed-5aa9-98f6-bcb6e68f2dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{10}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332999} :answer-field/id #uuid "34c562ed-e50c-5f34-9608-c043330e7886" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cc59b788-b5c5-5dc7-bac3-9ab39eac60d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-69893" :question/problem "![](images/be/be8468d84e3820bd1e9181d31aa3a1b7d1a85c743020a69cb67fc3f601a88363.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ec82676-385f-5f6a-ac9c-ba79308bee12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\text{ arccsc }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336316} {:answer/id #uuid "4b573896-b33b-57e6-b631-b759facddb70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336731} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee8c39b-aa90-5108-83c3-6a90312f3c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-4\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336894} {:answer/id #uuid "bcab4637-e9df-53b6-beca-07d40a0ec77c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337710} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ee07c5-6041-5304-9bfc-c6a2b63f065a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336731} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e3ae158-b764-50b7-b710-2eb3076e5cf8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bd957e59-0a76-5e62-9a01-c59f0b889410" :question/math-academy-id "q-71759" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "753fa037-4869-57bb-ac4a-0f8226e93dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337088} {:answer/id #uuid "7de44454-c056-5b46-a5ff-feadd65645cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337171} {:answer/id #uuid "af75991e-fe31-5097-bab1-f9f7833dfa8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337609} {:answer/id #uuid "cddee891-ba94-5bd0-9d64-b60f3812c423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337835} {:answer/id #uuid "f64bcadb-6519-5fea-93f7-63aa02c92d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337171} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a689b3-7d92-5c9d-b9a2-6c4b6c753f86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f5352827-e02f-55d1-bc3e-a103f93321ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-71761" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (8x-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (8x-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 8x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c05b9ce-0e54-531e-9602-9aa81d5949a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{5}+7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336447} {:answer/id #uuid "627ef198-a214-5417-80e9-b45a792ad5f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{5}+7\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336916} {:answer/id #uuid "71c35c47-7b7b-5fef-b294-b9cb841b489c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5{x}^{5}+7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337048} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6f9d28-d3e5-53a1-a5e5-29186ee63437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{5}+7\\text{ arccot }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337694} {:answer/id #uuid "edeaae97-ac2c-562a-abdb-dd6daecb94ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5{x}^{5}+7\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338111}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336447} :answer-field/id #uuid "31ce09db-263d-5513-8b14-b7d2cd24d8f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8482c878-eb98-5b38-8c38-4c3a4a08ab5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71768" :question/problem "If ${f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{4}+\\frac{7}{1+{x}^{2}},$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5{x}^{4}+\\frac{7}{1+{x}^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{7}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int {x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C \\\\  & ={x}^{5}+7\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "683d9e7c-61f6-5de6-abad-84dcf004875f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4\\text{ arcsin }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336963} {:answer/id #uuid "6a0882b7-a0a9-5289-b162-ca60fabaa466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-4\\text{ arcsin }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336972} {:answer/id #uuid "d8aeeeb4-e86e-575d-892e-520d2e23abb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-4\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337915} {:answer/id #uuid "f072d725-648f-5f34-a953-94bede93b280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338135} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cfd3a0-4ec2-51e0-bd20-788b4c0c89d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338221}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338221} :answer-field/id #uuid "55c2f8e1-3b8a-59cf-bd39-ca69a03b409c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "897f7448-7037-589b-bc8e-e9ffe322f46d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71774" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int (5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{4}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{4}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{4}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+4\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+4\\text{ arcsec }x+C \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4\\text{ arcsec }x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2af732f3-b0dc-5793-a81b-2631dc11f520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336435} {:answer/id #uuid "733c5a21-c647-52ab-a919-8a80bbbead81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\text{ arcsin }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337069} {:answer/id #uuid "75c8a2d2-a396-596b-8050-fe63de4a5851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\text{ arctan }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337091} {:answer/id #uuid "95948138-a8a6-5445-b9c9-fdd287efee17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\text{ arctan }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337398} {:answer/id #uuid "e59b54b8-9fef-5db5-8ace-2e476c52cf06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338036}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338036} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f257272-2f12-50ae-a6fd-7184a295f711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338567}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c37f5da7-d3e9-5087-b956-7bcf82e01ec3" :question/math-academy-id "q-71775" :question/problem "If ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{9}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}},$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(\\frac{9}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{9}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\text{ arcsec }x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338987 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ac67017-be7c-57ca-8eff-8f1738eb60c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336278} {:answer/id #uuid "1ac79ffd-e151-59ee-aec6-80ae5be82a9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336279} {:answer/id #uuid "2499f794-99b4-535d-b3e4-2d732c6de2a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336375} {:answer/id #uuid "326c547d-4f11-56c8-8b0a-a1f8ca3871c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336510} {:answer/id #uuid "75e66f64-6415-51e9-ad64-2c6bf754532e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+2arcsecx+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337094}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336279} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5067cfc-ddf9-52d7-bf38-073fd6987cc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c8649056-c397-51c3-956d-b54003524ff3" :question/math-academy-id "q-71779" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2{x}^{3}+2x+1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit  to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2{x}^{3}+2x+1}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{2x({x}^{2}+1)+1}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\cancel{({x}^{2}+1)}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}+1}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C,\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int x\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339005 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6de9ff01-0b1f-56cd-885f-31d83a6b64e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8x{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337007} {:answer/id #uuid "767d6034-4f15-5263-ac09-9c05f7472792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8{x}^{3}{e}^{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337099} {:answer/id #uuid "863405a3-9a66-5ca8-8f7d-483681a818bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}{e}^{8{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337245} {:answer/id #uuid "bbec19e9-c6de-585e-af2b-e55511e50cc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8{x}^{3}{e}^{2{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337701} {:answer/id #uuid "dcd7048a-7f6e-500d-bd2e-6421b3f20cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}{e}^{2{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337952}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337701} :answer-field/id #uuid "19f83298-fbd1-5427-81bb-2dc30205845b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "44577a72-fe3b-5755-87e3-6deb6a748e27" :question/math-academy-id "q-71873" :question/problem "Given that $y={e}^{2{x}^{4}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={e}^{u},\\,u=2{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (8{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =8{x}^{3}{e}^{u} \\\\  & =8{x}^{3}{e}^{2{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
